# Copy this file to .env.test.local and fill in your Supabase project's
# service_role key (Project Settings -> API in the Supabase dashboard).
#
# Deliberately a SEPARATE file from .env, not an addition to it: .env's own
# EXPO_PUBLIC_ variables get bundled into the client app by Expo, and the
# service_role key must never reach client-side code — it bypasses Row
# Level Security entirely (see .env.example's own warning). This file has
# no EXPO_PUBLIC_ prefix and is read only by Node-side E2E test setup
# (e2e/support/adminAuth.ts), never by the app itself.
#
# Used only to stand in for actions a browser-only E2E run genuinely cannot
# perform — confirming a signup's email (no real inbox to click a link in)
# and minting a pre-confirmed fixture account to sign in with. Real UI
# drives everything else. Git-ignored (matches .env.*.local) — never commit
# the real key.

SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=your-service-role-key
